hey guys today we're gonna explain the  quirk and philosophy of crust who is the  number six pro hero in Japan and has  likely shed more tears than 99% of the  characters in this series he was first  introduced to us during the pro hero arc  but it wasn't until much later in the  manga that we finally saw the full  capabilities of his power for that  reason this video is split into three  parts with the first part explaining his  abilities without giving away any plot  spoilers and then I'll briefly touch on  what we know if his personality and his  philosophy before moving on to the final  part which is a more spoiler a  discussion about what he's done in this  series so far so if it all sounds good  then be sure to hit that button and  let's get into it  cross has a very useful quirk known as  shield and this can be used for both  defensive maneuvers like Kirishima or  potentially offensive attacks like  Captain America starting at a basic  level the shield's he produces from his  body are made from thick crust on his  skin and because he can manifest it  anywhere the crust is frequently used to  protect his exposed areas his costume  design seems to be at least partly  inspired by the Spartans and therefore  it leaves quite a bit of his skin  uncovered during battles so this  defensive ability comes in pretty handy  the interesting thing about this quirk  is that it goes beyond just defending  the person who has it as crust can  extend his shields to protect or attack  anyone who's in his general area in the  manga he has a super move called shoot  shield and now this is where he grows a  detachable shield and then throws it  directly at his opponents the character  he used this on was incredibly powerful  so it's definitely not a move you should  underestimate another attacking move  that he has is when he grows these  jagged shields on his forearms and then  digs them into an enemy whilst they're  still digging into that person he then  has the option to instantly grow them to  a ridiculously large size crust has used  these jagged shields to dig into quite a  few people at this point and we've also  seen that he can manifest them just  around his hands instead anyway moving  back to his more defensive moves he can  extend his hands outwards and then  expand his shields to protect anyone  within a reasonable distance I thought  it was a pretty cool design choice like  the way they all connect and as you can  see it all originates from his hand here  if he was to do this with both hands at  the same time I would imagine that he  could create the Great Wall of China but  you know what that's just my opinion  I consider cross quark to be a more  versatile version of Kirishima sand I'll  explain why  looking at their quirks rather than them  as an individual I think shield can do  more things obviously it gives  protection to the user's body as well as  their allies and it also provides attack  options from both close and long range  whereas with hardening although it might  potentially be tougher and like harder  so far it's purely limited to protecting  the user's individual body and also  providing additional damage for close  range attacks so that's why I say cross  quote is a more versatile version  because it can do a lot more but that  doesn't necessarily mean it's better I  mean we still have yet to see her she  miss full potential I would be  interested to know how tough this crust  is versus a care team is unbreakable  form moving on to his personality now  crust is a very empathetic and  passionate character in his first ever  appearance he let the crowd know his  pain and not being able to be there  during all front attack at Camino and he  has tears in his eyes at the fort of  Almighty retirement this shows us many  things I mean the main thing is that  he's not someone who would shy away from  dangerous or life-threatening situations  and he actively beats himself up if he  can't help out his fellow heroes cross  was the only hero that I've known so far  who genuinely actually shows sympathy  for the no move nevertheless he doesn't  let that get in the way of the actual  mission at hand from what I can remember  and I may I may be wrong but from what I  can think of I can't think of another  hero who's ever like made that  connection like oh yeah the gnome who  used to be human I don't like killing  humans so I feel bad killing this no  move like I've never heard another hero  from what I can remember at least going  through that same train of thought based  on that and you know how in tune he is  with his emotions I would definitely  describe him as a chivalrous hero based  on everything we've seen so it's just  one of many reasons why Kirishima should  intern with him make it happen her ago  she make it happen but would that  explained let's move on to part three of  the video where I'll be looking at his  heroic actions during the most recent  arc of the manga so if you don't want to  know any spoilers then this right here  is your 5 second warning during the war  arc there were these six no moves  blocking cross paths and he activates  these jagged shields on the back of his  hands like I mentioned earlier and then  proceeds to butch these guys pretty  quickly but you know six of them six in  a cramped hallway but only a top hero is  dispatching them that  so kudos to crust on that one just a  couple pages later he's already further  down the hallway and comes face to face  with the higher nomu like I said earlier  in the video but with much less detail  when he expanded his shields to attack  this high in nomu look how thick the  shields are in this moment like it's  crazy  time and time again like crust and his  quirk has come in so useful during this  arc and although it Mittal ehi wasn't  able to defeat this no mood we have to  consider the fact that it does have  super heat generation so we've got to  give the guy a break on that one also  when he used the shoot shield attack on  this higher nomu here can we just  appreciate how massive this thing  actually is here is that same gnome  who's standing in front of present Mike  and it's leg alone is the size of two  fully grown men and just for cross to  throw a frisbee made of his skin you  know or as crust is pretty insane  because we haven't seen his no more  sense this is definitely a quirk that  would have required intense training to  get it to where it is today in his days  as a student like I wouldn't really be  surprised if all he could do then was  manifest the crust over his skin in much  the same way that Kirishima is only able  to harden his skin all this other stuff  like the elaborate shields or the Noma  busting attacks like that will probably  came with time and experience which is  one of many reasons why I would love to  see the current class 1-a  as adults like when we can see their  full potential anyway guys that was my  quick video on cross quirk and  personality explained I hope you enjoyed  it and be sure to subscribe as I have a  video I'm planning about my favorite  quirks in the war arc of the manga do be  sure to check that out when it releases  peace out
 

